-          <t indent="0" pn="section-4.2.3-106"><artwork name="" type="" align="left" alt=""><![CDATA[
-      4.2.3.9.         HELLO
-]]></artwork>
-</t>
-          <t indent="0" pn="section-4.2.3-107"><artwork name="" type="" align="left" alt=""><![CDATA[
-         HELLO (OpCode = 9) is used as part of the ST failure
-         detection mechanism; see Section 3.7.1.2 (page 49).
-]]></artwork>
-</t>
-          <t indent="0" pn="section-4.2.3-108"><artwork name="" type="" align="left" alt=""><![CDATA[
-            R (bit 8) is used for the Restarted bit.
-]]></artwork>
-</t>
-          <t indent="0" pn="section-4.2.3-109"><artwork name="" type="" align="left" alt=""><![CDATA[
-            Reference is non-zero to inform the receiver that an ACK
-            should be promptly sent so that the sender can update its
-            round-trip time estimates.  If the Reference is zero, no
-            ACK should be sent.
-]]></artwork>
-</t>
